<section vertical-align="center" id="bbs026" image-layout="blank"><card-template-instructions>The dense brief: a working title and two columns of body text at close to equal length, with a source caption; the card for the paragraph that cannot be cut, carried by column balance rather than smaller type.</card-template-instructions><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="vopxS3tKRc"><h2>What the customer review told us</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item colspan="30" id="i4U3VihAJz"><p>We spoke with 24 accounts in June, split evenly across the four regions and weighted toward customers whose order frequency changed during the quarter. The interviews were thirty minutes each and followed the same five questions on ordering, delivery, stock, pricing and service.</p><p>Ordering and delivery drew the most comment. Sixteen accounts named the second delivery day as the single most useful change of the year, and eleven said it had reduced the stock they hold.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="30" id="Bi6g5Ogt-U"><p>Pricing drew the least comment, which we read as acceptance rather than enthusiasm; three accounts asked for volume tiers on the new lines. Service comments centered on the phone line, where hold times rose during the warehouse move and have since returned to the target.</p><p>Two accounts raised packaging waste on the smaller, more frequent deliveries. Operations is testing returnable crates with both accounts in the third quarter.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm">Source: customer review interviews, June 2 to June 20, 2026; 24 accounts, four regions.</p></grid-item></grid></section>